            <pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:44:39 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>52</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.20</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>Opening a folder right after naming it no longer fails on network</b> shares.<b> New Folder ▸ type a name ▸ Enter ▸ Enter reported</b> "“untitled folder” can't be found" on SMB volumes. The rename had already succeeded, but the listing still carried the pre-rename URL until the folder re-read finished — long enough over SMB for the second Enter to navigate to a name that no longer existed. A completed rename now updates the listing immediately, and an Enter that arrives while the rename is still in flight waits for it instead of opening the old row. A rejected rename (name already taken) reports as before and opens nothing.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
